  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35568452",
      "title": "What is Interface",
      "lectureOrder": 75,
      "videoOrder": 74,
      "sourceHash": "38136419350c57e6dc94252952fcf1477444d438631833962e6c73b4441d1b69",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.15,
          "end": 3.18,
          "en": "-: In this video, we'll talk about interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.18,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "Now, before we start with interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 6.81,
          "en": "let's talk about the abstract class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.81,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "Now, let's say I create abstract class here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 11.13,
          "en": "So we'll say abstract class A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.13,
          "end": 14.76,
          "en": "And in this class, let me create some methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.76,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "Now, we all know in the abstract class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 20.04,
          "en": "we can create abstract methods and normal methods as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "But let's say if I have abstract class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "which only has let's say abstract methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 28.05,
          "en": "if I say public abstract void show,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.05,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "and we have public abstract void config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "Now, when you have abstract class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 35.73,
          "en": "with two abstract methods, of course this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 38.58,
          "en": "There's no compulsion to have non-abstract methods here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.58,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "or we call them as concrete methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 41.61,
          "en": "There's no need for them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.61,
          "end": 43.29,
          "en": "Now, when you have a situation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.29,
          "end": 45.18,
          "en": "where you have abstract class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 45.18,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "which only has abstract methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "we have another way of doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "Now see, all this are decided at design time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 54.12,
          "en": "So when you make an application at designing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 54.12,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "you specify things, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 57.99,
          "en": "What are the classes I need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 57.99,
          "end": 60.3,
          "en": "and what are the abstract class we need?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 60.3,
          "end": 62.37,
          "en": "So you create this hierarchy of system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "Of course we'll talk about that hierarchy in some time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "Why do we need it? But at this point, we create a hierarchy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "And when you have a class which only has abstract methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 73.14,
          "en": "the other alternative for that is to create a interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 73.14,
          "end": 74.82,
          "en": "So instead of creating an abstract class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 74.82,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "we can create an interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 79.28999999999999,
          "en": "Most of the time we use this interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 79.28999999999999,
          "end": 80.58,
          "en": "in project development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 80.58,
          "end": 83.25,
          "en": "So let's understand that. So we have the interface A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 83.25,
          "end": 85.56,
          "en": "Now you will say, what is changing there?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 85.56,
          "end": 87.95,
          "en": "Now, first of all, interface is not a class, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 87.95,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "So that's why that's the main difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 91.71000000000001,
          "en": "between abstract class and interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 91.71000000000001,
          "end": 92.88,
          "en": "And by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 96.6,
          "en": "every method in the interface is public abstract.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 96.6,
          "end": 98.67,
          "en": "So these two keywords actually not required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 98.67,
          "end": 100.38,
          "en": "because anyway they are public abstract.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 100.38,
          "end": 101.91,
          "en": "So even if you don't mention,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 101.91,
          "end": 104.03999999999999,
          "en": "they are by default public abstract.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 104.03999999999999,
          "end": 105.42,
          "en": "And that's why, if you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 105.42,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "when I put a semicolon just after the method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "there is no error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 112.62,
          "en": "because behind the scene, public abstract is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "Now this is your interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "So interface basically means it's like a class, just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 122.6,
          "en": "that all the methods are by default, public abstract, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 122.7,
          "end": 125.55,
          "en": "But then how will I use this? How will I instantiate this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 125.55,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "The same problem was there with abstract class, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 129.72,
          "en": "We cannot instantiate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 129.72,
          "end": 132.03,
          "en": "Now, if you look at this, how do I instantiate? Let's try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 132.03,
          "end": 134.52,
          "en": "So I will say A obj.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "See, there's no problem in creating a reference of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 140.13,
          "en": "So that also means we are creating a type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 140.13,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "the way you create classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 144.36,
          "en": "So let's say if A is a class, you can say A obj.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 144.36,
          "end": 145.65,
          "en": "So A is a type, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 145.65,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "In the same way here, the interface A is a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 150.78,
          "en": "Okay, this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 150.78,
          "end": 154.29,
          "en": "But now when you try to create object for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 154.29,
          "end": 155.91,
          "en": "it will give you an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 155.91,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "It says if you see the error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 160.32,
          "en": "it says \"Cannot instantiate the type A,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 160.32,
          "end": 163.26,
          "en": "because it's interface, you can't instantiate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 165.48,
          "en": "Okay, then what's the solution?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 165.48,
          "end": 167.1,
          "en": "The solution is, see, first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 167.1,
          "end": 168.15,
          "en": "why do we create interface?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 168.15,
          "end": 170.16,
          "en": "We create interface so that we can design something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 171.6,
          "en": "We can say, example, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "if you ask me about how do we create a table,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 178.92000000000002,
          "en": "I can say, or maybe if you ask me how to reach somewhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 178.92000000000002,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "so I can say, \"Go straight, take a right, go straight,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 183.99,
          "en": "take a right, take an auto, take a bus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 185.25,
          "en": "get down at the next stop.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 185.25,
          "end": 187.56,
          "en": "So what I'm doing is I'm giving you the path, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 187.56,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "I'm giving you design. You have to literally take a walk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 194.22,
          "en": "I will not walk for you. I will just show the directions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 194.22,
          "end": 196.027,
          "en": "In the same way, interface says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 196.027,
          "end": 199.62,
          "en": "\"I will tell you what are the methods you need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 199.62,
          "end": 201.06,
          "en": "but I will not implement them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 201.06,
          "end": 202.65,
          "en": "It is your job to implement.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "So when I say your, now I'm talking about classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "See, ultimately you create object of a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 211.77,
          "en": "interface just show you the design.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 211.77,
          "end": 213.6,
          "en": "So here, what I can do is I can create a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 213.6,
          "end": 214.82999999999998,
          "en": "let's say class B.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 214.82999999999998,
          "end": 216.18,
          "en": "So we have a class B here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 216.18,
          "end": 217.44,
          "en": "And then in this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 217.44,
          "end": 220.26,
          "en": "I want to implement these two methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 223.38,
          "en": "Now, in terms of abstract class, we say extends, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 223.38,
          "end": 226.23,
          "en": "Because class extends another class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 226.23,
          "end": 228.15,
          "en": "Here A is the interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 228.15,
          "end": 230.1,
          "en": "We have to use a different keyword here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 230.1,
          "end": 232.11,
          "en": "The keyword which we use is implements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 234.78,
          "en": "So whenever you want to implement the interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 234.78,
          "end": 237.03,
          "en": "you say implements keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 237.03,
          "end": 240.33,
          "en": "And when you say implements, it becomes compulsory for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 240.33,
          "end": 242.82,
          "en": "to define both the methods, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 242.82,
          "end": 244.77,
          "en": "If you fail to define both the methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 248.64,
          "en": "by default, your class also becomes abstract, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 248.64,
          "end": 250.02,
          "en": "But we don't want to create abstract class, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 250.02,
          "end": 251.67,
          "en": "We want to create a concrete class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 251.67,
          "end": 253.65,
          "en": "We want to create object of B.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 253.65,
          "end": 258.54,
          "en": "In that case, it's your job to define both the methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 258.54,
          "end": 260.58,
          "en": "Okay, there's one way you can use a shortcut here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 260.58,
          "end": 262.44,
          "en": "You can just go back here and say Quick Fix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 262.44,
          "end": 264.72,
          "en": "It will ask you to implement the methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 264.72,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "or you can do the hard work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "You can say public void show.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 270.39,
          "en": "And then you can define something here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 270.39,
          "end": 273.18,
          "en": "I can say I'm defining in show.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 273.18,
          "end": 275.25,
          "en": "And then we can define another method as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 275.25,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "which is config or public void config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 282.69,
          "en": "And here we can define in config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 282.69,
          "end": 283.89,
          "en": "So basically what you're doing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 283.89,
          "end": 286.86,
          "en": "you are implementing both the methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 286.86,
          "end": 287.693,
          "en": "As I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 287.693,
          "end": 289.86,
          "en": "if you fail to implement these methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 289.86,
          "end": 291.81,
          "en": "this class becomes an abstract class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 291.81,
          "end": 293.52,
          "en": "but we are implementing it, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 294.45,
          "en": "Now, when you implement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 294.45,
          "end": 297.45,
          "en": "basically you can't create object of A,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 297.45,
          "end": 302.45,
          "en": "but you can create object of B, and you can see it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 302.52,
          "end": 306.45,
          "en": "And now using this obj I can call show.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 306.45,
          "end": 310.11,
          "en": "I can call, what other method we have? We have config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 310.11,
          "end": 312.9,
          "en": "So we can call both the methods and that perfectly works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 312.9,
          "end": 314.49,
          "en": "If I compile and run this code,",
